# FILE LAW — Website vs .oo/.oot only
File: website/audit/file-law.oot

Verdict: FAIL on residual deploy types. PASS on the 256-line
cap and on new docs this pass. Written 2026-09-04 after the
split, .oot pulls, and header repair.

## 1. Observed file types

GitHub Pages must serve HTML, CSS, and JS. That residual is
the deploy surface. New product docs in this repo are `.oot`.
Do not add more `.js`, `.json`, or `.md`.

`install.sh` is a third host script (RULES.oot §1.14 allows
two). Keep the `/install.sh` URL. Do not grow the file.

`README.md` is this repo's GitHub front door. Governance
README.md is the only other allowed `.md` in the org.

## 2. Line cap (RULES 1.8, RFC-0003)

Every `.oo`, `.oot`, and residual `.js` file is at most 256
lines. `src/dogfight/cca.js` is the tightest at 254.

`index.html` holds the no-JS home body and stays under 256.
`styles/main.css` is one stylesheet and stays under 256.

## 3. Academy headers (RFC-0003 §2)

Product `.oo` files use Title, Logline, Setup, Beats.
Setup was restored on `assets/ANCHOR.oo`, `styles/ANCHOR.oo`,
and `.github/workflows/ANCHOR.oo`. Residual `.js` files keep
a short Title and Logline.

## 4. Honest model

1. Source of truth: `.oot` copy and `.oo` indexes.
2. Deploy residual: `index.html`, `404.html`, `styles/main.css`,
   `src/**/*.js`. No generator yet.
3. Do not mark those files GENERATED. They are hand-maintained.

Until oodac emits the page, do not add a second stylesheet or
a new `.js` file except to split an over-cap file.

## 5. Next repair

None in this repo for file law. Do not convert the dogfight
to `.oo` until a JS emitter exists.
